 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did a copy of the Cardiff Giant beat the original fake?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.905
  },
  {
   "text": "Two farmhands dig a well, and their shovels hit a stone foot.",
   "s": 3.205,
   "e": 5.921
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a leg. Then a ten-foot stone man, curled up like he's asleep.",
   "s": 6.121,
   "e": 9.169
  },
  {
   "text": "People call it a petrified giant, so they line up for miles to see it.",
   "s": 9.369,
   "e": 12.788
  },
  {
   "text": "The farmer throws up a tent and charges fifty cents a look.",
   "s": 12.988,
   "e": 15.763
  },
  {
   "text": "Thousands come every day, and wagons jam the roads!",
   "s": 15.963,
   "e": 18.161
  },
  {
   "text": "Scientists call it a carved statue. Nobody listens.",
   "s": 18.361,
   "e": 20.975
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it gets weirder. P.T. Barnum offers fifty thousand dollars to rent the giant.",
   "s": 21.175,
   "e": 25.392
  },
  {
   "text": "The owners say no, so Barnum builds his own giant out of plaster!",
   "s": 25.592,
   "e": 28.859
  },
  {
   "text": "He shows it in New York and swears his is the real one.",
   "s": 29.059,
   "e": 31.677
  },
  {
   "text": "And more people pay to see Barnum's copy than the original.",
   "s": 32.077,
   "e": 34.766
  },
  {
   "text": "Because the first giant was fake too. George Hull had it carved and buried.",
   "s": 34.966,
   "e": 38.507
  },
  {
   "text": "Hull's joke made him rich, and Barnum's copy of the joke made him richer.",
   "s": 38.707,
   "e": 42.082
  },
  {
   "text": "So which giant was the real fake?",
   "s": 42.282,
   "e": 43.921
  }
 ],
